<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frédéric Maurice de La Tour d'Auvergne</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1605–1652</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Duke of Bouillon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frédéric Maurice de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-la-tour-dauvergne">La Tour d'Auvergne</a>, Duke of Bouillon and Prince of Sedan, was the elder brother of Marshal Turenne. He repeatedly conspired against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cardinal-richelieu">Cardinal Richelieu</a>, and after joining the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henri-coiffier-de-ruze-marquis-of-cinq-mars">Cinq-Mars</a> plot in 1642 he saved his life by surrendering Sedan to the French crown. He later took part in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-fronde">Fronde</a> and received French estates in exchange for his principality.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederic-maurice-de-la-tour-dauvergne.jpg" alt="Frédéric Maurice de La Tour d'Auvergne" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michiel Jansz. van Mierevelt · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Michiel_van_Mierevelt,_hertog_van_Bouillon_(1626).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
